title: Tardy - Meeting Bar Foundation
status: draft
created: 2026-08-07
author: Luke Carrier
context: Tardy is a Linux analogue of the Meeting Bar app usually seen on macOS. It keeps sight of the user's upcoming meetings and offers a single control to jump straight into whichever meeting service hosts a given meeting. Tardy presents two views of the same surface. A persistent overlay sits above the user's other windows so the schedule is never missed. A compact one-line summary sits in the desktop's status area for at-a-glance awareness, with a fuller day-grouped tooltip behind it. The user's meetings come from the calendar accounts they have already registered on the machine, so Tardy works with whatever calendar setup the desktop already knows about rather than requiring the user to configure or authorise anything new inside the app. A meeting's join control always opens the correct service for that meeting, no matter which provider is hosting it. All-day entries such as holidays, out-of-office and birthdays are schedule context rather than something to join, so they belong in the tooltip only and must never claim the one-line summary or interrupt the user with an overlay.
problem: The user frequently runs late to meetings because there is no lightweight at-a-glance view of the day's meetings on their desktop with one-click join
goals[3]:
  - Surface the user's upcoming meetings for a configurable lookahead window
  - Provide a persistent overlay above all windows with a per-meeting join control
  - Keep the user informed without any per-app account setup; the machine's existing calendars are used as-is
nonGoals[3]:
  - This ADR covers the foundation only, not packed distribution or packaging
  - No modification of the user's calendars; Tardy only reads them
  - No in-app login or credential entry; only calendars the desktop already knows are surfaced
requirements[8]{id,title,slug,description}:
  FR-001,Show Upcoming Meetings,show-upcoming-meetings,"The app displays the user's meetings from the calendar accounts available on the machine, restricted to a configurable lookahead window"
  FR-002,Configurable Lookahead,lookahead-days,"The user can configure how many days ahead meetings are shown, defaulting to 5 days"
  FR-003,Height Over Other Windows,overlay-above,"A persistent on-screen panel shows the meetings and stays above all other windows on every attached display"
  FR-004,Join A Meeting,join-meeting,"Each meeting offers a control that launches the meeting, opening the correct service regardless of the conference provider"
  FR-005,Text Status Summary,status-summary,"The app maintains a short text summary of the current or next meeting for display in the desktop status area, backed by a day-grouped tooltip listing the whole lookahead window"
  FR-006,Automatic Refresh,automatic-refresh,"Upcoming meetings refresh automatically so that the panel promptly reflects new, changed or started meetings, including a meeting approaching its start time"
  FR-007,Meeting Without A Link,no-link,"A meeting that offers no usable join link is still shown, with its join control visibly disabled"
  FR-008,All-Day Events In Tooltip Only,all-day-tooltip-only,"All-day events are listed in the tooltip alongside timed meetings, but are never chosen as the current or next meeting in the one-line status summary and never trigger the overlay"
nonFunctional[3]{id,title,slug,description}:
  NFR-001,Provider Agnostic,provider-agnostic,"Joining works for the meeting services the user's calendars reference, not only for one specific vendor"
  NFR-002,Runs Without New Auth,no-new-auth,"The app runs using the calendar credentials the desktop already holds; it surfaces what it can even when one account's calendar cannot be reached and it never demand that the user enter a fresh sign-in solely for Tardy"
  NFR-003,Resilient To Missing Data,resilient,"If a calendar account cannot be read the app stays up, continues to show the calendars it can, and recovers once the blocked account is available"
acceptance[6]{id,title,slug,description}:
  AC-001,Shows Registered Calendars,shows-calendars,"With a desktop-confirmed Google calendar, the app enumerates and shows that calendar's meetings for the lookahead window"
  AC-002,Join Opens Service,join-opens-service,"Activating a meeting's join control launches the meeting's own service such that the user lands in the meeting"
  AC-003,Overlay Raised Amply,overlay-raised,"The panel is visible above all other windows on each attached display without any interleaving window action"
  AC-004,Lookahead Configurable,lookahead-configurable,"Changing the configured lookahead changes the set of meetings surfaced"
  AC-005,Unavailable Account Safe,unavailable-account-safe,"With a calendar account that cannot be refreshed, the app stays functional, shows an explicit empty state, and recovers when the account is back"
  AC-006,All-Day Event Stays In Tooltip,all-day-tooltip-verified,"With an all-day event spanning a day that also holds a timed meeting, the tooltip lists both, the one-line summary shows only the timed meeting, and the all-day event raises no overlay when its day begins"
edgeCases[4]{id,title,slug,description}:
  EC-001,No Calendars Available,no-calendars,"The panel and the status summary both show a clear empty state and remain ready to update"
  EC-002,Meeting Without A Link,meeting-no-link,"If a meeting cannot yield a usable join link its join control is disabled but the meeting is still shown"
  EC-003,Account Drops Mid-Refresh,account-drop,"When a calendar account becomes unavailable at refresh time the partial list from the other calendars is still shown and the account is retried"
  EC-004,Only All-Day Events Ahead,all-day-only,"When the lookahead window holds nothing but all-day events the tooltip still lists them while the one-line summary shows its empty state and no overlay is raised"